.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1213 PM PDT Sun Oct 4 2026
(Tuesday through next Saturday)

The ridging persists for the next few days and as previously
mentioned, the Heat Advisory extends to Wednesday night for the
inland and Bayshore regions. Temperatures across the inland valleys
remain in the middle 90s to near 105 through Wednesday. Along the
Pacific, we continue to monitor how the forecast trends evolve as
impacts from a shallow marine layer or stronger onshore flow than
the current forecast may significantly impact the immediate coast.

A pattern change will begin Thursday as the ridge flattens and
troughing develops in the northeastern Pacific and moves into
southwestern Canada and the western United States. This will start a
cooling trend with most locations dropping out of Moderate HeatRisk
by Friday. Ensemble model cluster analysis hints at significant
uncertainty for the upcoming weekend and the early part of the
upcoming week regarding the strength of the trough and how long it
could persist.

