.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1029 AM PDT Sun Oct 4 2026

VFR conditions regionwide throughout much of the day with light
onshore winds forecast to return by mid-afternoon. Winds begin to
diminish after sunset and more so into Monday morning. The
greatest potential for low ceilings and/or fog to occur Monday
morning will be at coastal sites (MRY, HAF, and to a lesser extent
SNS) as high cloud cover is forecast to diminish throughout the
day. However, confidence is low-to-moderate for fog development in
these locations.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Weak offshore winds currently with weak to
moderate onshore flow expected by mid-afternoon. Winds ease
overnight and into early Monday morning with generally high
confidence of VFR conditions persisting through the TAF period.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Light drainage winds currently at
SNS will shift onshore by early afternoon and prevail before
easing after sunset. The greatest potential for sub-IFR conditions
will be at MRY early Monday morning, less confidence for SNS. Any
low clouds and/or fog that does develop is likely to dissipate by
16Z Monday.

