.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 405 AM PDT Sun Oct 4 2026

Hot and dry conditions will continue through Thursday, which will
be accompanied with weak offshore flow. Poor to very poor
overnight recovery is expected for the thermal belts, generally
for elevations above 1000-1500 feet, leading to elevated fire
weather conditions. The marine layer is expected to be confined to
the immediate coast and around 500 feet. If working in the
thermal belts, Moderate to Extreme HeatRisk is forecast this week,
with temperature and HeatRisk trends improving late week. A
pattern change is expected late in the week or over the weekend.
Cooler weather and the potential for improved RH recovery is
forecast or Friday.

